{"duration_api_ms":612507,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5c9c4781-863e-4543-a3de-cfd897ac5cd1","total_cost_usd":1.6506892000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":144,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80240,"cache_read_input_tokens":4525046,"output_tokens":42029,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2419,"cache_read_input_tokens":94778,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2486},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4037,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004142,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":144,"outputTokens":42029,"cacheReadInputTokens":4525046,"cacheCreationInputTokens":80240,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.6465472000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10264,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":73,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Set up HTTPS on node1:8443 via nginx with certificates auto-renewed by a cron-driven script before expiry, and confirmed nginx picks up each renewed certificate via a graceful reload with zero downtime. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol on node1 with verified boot-identity change and full post-restart recovery, including a live cron-triggered renewal after reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed nginx and cronie on node1 (RHEL 9)\",\"Created a self-signed root CA at /etc/pki/rotation-ca (10-year validity)\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: checks server cert expiry via openssl x509 -checkend 180, issues a fresh CA-signed cert (5 min validity, SANs for node1/NODE_IP/loopback) when within 180s of expiry, atomically replaces key/cert, restores SELinux cert_t context, and gracefully reloads nginx (nginx -s reload) only after nginx -t passes\",\"Fixed an SELinux mislabeling issue via semanage fcontext + restorecon for /etc/pki/rotation-cert and /etc/pki/rotation-ca\",\"Fixed a cron PATH bug: cron's minimal PATH (/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin) omitted /usr/sbin, silently breaking restorecon and nginx reload under cron; switched to absolute paths for both\",\"Deployed nginx server block listening on 0.0.0.0:8443 and [::]:8443 with ssl_certificate/ssl_certificate_key pointing at the rotated cert/key paths\",\"Installed /etc/cron.d/renew-cert running the renewal script every minute via crond\",\"Enabled and started nginx and crond as persistent systemd services\",\"Observed a full automatic renewal cycle live: cert serial rotated (...CF4D -> ...CF4E) exactly at the cron-triggered reload while continuously polling HTTPS every second with zero non-200 responses\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline on node1: boot_id, uptime -s, service states, cert dates/serial, HTTPS 200\",\"Restarted node1 via systemctl reboot (acknowledgement returned before disconnect), polled until exec was available again\",\"Verified changed boot_id and new uptime -s timestamp on node1 post-restart, proving a genuine reboot\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: nginx and crond active, cert files retained correct SELinux labels, HTTPS answering 200, and a fresh cron-triggered renewal (...CF4E -> ...CF4F) fired on schedule after reboot with zero downtime observed throughout\",\"Cleaned up temporary watch/log files on node1\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"HTTPS served on port 8443\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ec1e38b0d78247dd\",\"cmd-0eea9f01eb3b46bc\"],\"summary\":\"nginx config for 8443 deployed; curl to https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns http_code=200 and openssl s_client confirms cert served with matching dates/serial.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-014dd29b4dff4dcd\",\"cmd-e0297f8c037b432e\"],\"summary\":\"journalctl -t renew-cert shows cron-triggered 'issued new cert' events occurring every ~2 minutes, well before the 5-minute cert lifetime elapses (renewal threshold 180s remaining).\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (root cause fix)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ae249f11716c4db2\",\"cmd-e0297f8c037b432e\",\"cmd-614aec6ce2fc4fc5\"],\"summary\":\"Diagnosed why nginx wasn't reloading (SELinux tmp_t label denial, then cron PATH lacking /usr/sbin for restorecon/nginx); fixed by using absolute paths, confirmed manual run performs full issue+restorecon+nginx -t+reload successfully.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Live proof of zero-downtime renewal (pre-restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2ff1cb3422be4089\",\"cmd-32e095f84faf4c51\",\"cmd-eaa34ca393984207\"],\"summary\":\"1-second-interval HTTPS polling log shows cert serial transition from ...CF4D (84 consecutive 200s) to ...CF4E (24 consecutive 200s) exactly at the cron-triggered reload, with zero non-200 responses across the whole window.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3627dd483fc04741\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 583ddd53-..., uptime -s 2026-09-04 23:36:54, nginx/crond active+enabled, valid cert, HTTPS 200, and recent renewal log entries before rebooting.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c0fc2bf2b1f147cf\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot was backgrounded with a 2s delay via nohup so the exec call returned its acknowledgement (PID) before the node dropped off.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 boot identity changed after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-720e2b5af3ac47ea\",\"cmd-19f3c88fc4f84fad\",\"cmd-d9a14bb2572f4079\",\"cmd-8a577180d49b4b55\"],\"summary\":\"Connection was lost (confirming the node actually went down) then polled until exec succeeded again; boot_id changed from 583ddd53-... to 3c674d6d-..., and uptime -s advanced to 2026-09-04 23:51:50, proving a genuine reboot rather than a service restart.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services and data on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ac483b4439cf4e6f\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, nginx and crond are active, the previously issued cert persisted with correct SELinux cert_t labels, HTTPS answers 200, and the cron renewal schedule file is intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart proof that automatic renewal and zero-downtime reload still function\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4cefad40b8284b66\",\"cmd-588650339c9f4bc2\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, a new cron-triggered renewal fired on schedule (serial ...CF4E -> ...CF4F) with the renew-cert log showing 'issued new cert'/'nginx reloaded', and the 1s-interval HTTPS watch log shows zero non-200 responses across the transition.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Set up HTTPS on node1:8443 via nginx with certificates auto-renewed by a cron-driven script before expiry, and confirmed nginx picks up each renewed certificate via a graceful reload with zero downtime. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol on node1 with verified boot-identity change and full post-restart recovery, including a live cron-triggered renewal after reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed nginx and cronie on node1 (RHEL 9)","Created a self-signed root CA at /etc/pki/rotation-ca (10-year validity)","Wrote /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: checks server cert expiry via openssl x509 -checkend 180, issues a fresh CA-signed cert (5 min validity, SANs for node1/NODE_IP/loopback) when within 180s of expiry, atomically replaces key/cert, restores SELinux cert_t context, and gracefully reloads nginx (nginx -s reload) only after nginx -t passes","Fixed an SELinux mislabeling issue via semanage fcontext + restorecon for /etc/pki/rotation-cert and /etc/pki/rotation-ca","Fixed a cron PATH bug: cron's minimal PATH (/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin) omitted /usr/sbin, silently breaking restorecon and nginx reload under cron; switched to absolute paths for both","Deployed nginx server block listening on 0.0.0.0:8443 and [::]:8443 with ssl_certificate/ssl_certificate_key pointing at the rotated cert/key paths","Installed /etc/cron.d/renew-cert running the renewal script every minute via crond","Enabled and started nginx and crond as persistent systemd services","Observed a full automatic renewal cycle live: cert serial rotated (...CF4D -> ...CF4E) exactly at the cron-triggered reload while continuously polling HTTPS every second with zero non-200 responses","Captured pre-restart baseline on node1: boot_id, uptime -s, service states, cert dates/serial, HTTPS 200","Restarted node1 via systemctl reboot (acknowledgement returned before disconnect), polled until exec was available again","Verified changed boot_id and new uptime -s timestamp on node1 post-restart, proving a genuine reboot","Verified post-restart recovery: nginx and crond active, cert files retained correct SELinux labels, HTTPS answering 200, and a fresh cron-triggered renewal (...CF4E -> ...CF4F) fired on schedule after reboot with zero downtime observed throughout","Cleaned up temporary watch/log files on node1"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS served on port 8443","command_ids":["cmd-ec1e38b0d78247dd","cmd-0eea9f01eb3b46bc"],"summary":"nginx config for 8443 deployed; curl to https://$NODE_IP:8443/ returns http_code=200 and openssl s_client confirms cert served with matching dates/serial."},{"requirement":"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry","command_ids":["cmd-014dd29b4dff4dcd","cmd-e0297f8c037b432e"],"summary":"journalctl -t renew-cert shows cron-triggered 'issued new cert' events occurring every ~2 minutes, well before the 5-minute cert lifetime elapses (renewal threshold 180s remaining)."},{"requirement":"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests (root cause fix)","command_ids":["cmd-ae249f11716c4db2","cmd-e0297f8c037b432e","cmd-614aec6ce2fc4fc5"],"summary":"Diagnosed why nginx wasn't reloading (SELinux tmp_t label denial, then cron PATH lacking /usr/sbin for restorecon/nginx); fixed by using absolute paths, confirmed manual run performs full issue+restorecon+nginx -t+reload successfully."},{"requirement":"Live proof of zero-downtime renewal (pre-restart)","command_ids":["cmd-2ff1cb3422be4089","cmd-32e095f84faf4c51","cmd-eaa34ca393984207"],"summary":"1-second-interval HTTPS polling log shows cert serial transition from ...CF4D (84 consecutive 200s) to ...CF4E (24 consecutive 200s) exactly at the cron-triggered reload, with zero non-200 responses across the whole window."},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-3627dd483fc04741"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 583ddd53-..., uptime -s 2026-09-04 23:36:54, nginx/crond active+enabled, valid cert, HTTPS 200, and recent renewal log entries before rebooting."},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-c0fc2bf2b1f147cf"],"summary":"systemctl reboot was backgrounded with a 2s delay via nohup so the exec call returned its acknowledgement (PID) before the node dropped off."},{"requirement":"Node1 boot identity changed after restart","command_ids":["cmd-720e2b5af3ac47ea","cmd-19f3c88fc4f84fad","cmd-d9a14bb2572f4079","cmd-8a577180d49b4b55"],"summary":"Connection was lost (confirming the node actually went down) then polled until exec succeeded again; boot_id changed from 583ddd53-... to 3c674d6d-..., and uptime -s advanced to 2026-09-04 23:51:50, proving a genuine reboot rather than a service restart."},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required services and data on node1","command_ids":["cmd-ac483b4439cf4e6f"],"summary":"After reboot, nginx and crond are active, the previously issued cert persisted with correct SELinux cert_t labels, HTTPS answers 200, and the cron renewal schedule file is intact."},{"requirement":"Post-restart proof that automatic renewal and zero-downtime reload still function","command_ids":["cmd-4cefad40b8284b66","cmd-588650339c9f4bc2"],"summary":"After reboot, a new cron-triggered renewal fired on schedule (serial ...CF4E -> ...CF4F) with the renew-cert log showing 'issued new cert'/'nginx reloaded', and the 1s-interval HTTPS watch log shows zero non-200 responses across the transition."}]},"ttft_ms":10021,"type":"result","duration_ms":1046739,"uuid":"35f75513-72a6-4745-89d6-23666f9922fd","ttft_stream_ms":1183,"time_to_request_ms":41,"first_content_frame_ms":1779,"queued_turn_count":0}
